{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he is a witness, or saw, or knew</b> These are not three separate matters, for there is no witness without seeing and without knowledge. Rather, the verse says: if he heard the voice of an oath that was imposed upon him to adjure him concerning a matter in which he is a witness — whether by seeing or by knowledge — if he does not testify, he bears sin. Now, he is not liable for this offering unless he knows testimony that would prove successful from him for the one administering the oath in court. Therefore our Sages explained (Shevuot 33) that there is testimony that is effective through seeing without knowledge, and there is testimony that is effective through knowledge without seeing. How so? \"I counted out money for you in the presence of so-and-so and so-and-so,\" and the defendant claims, \"These things never happened\" — they come and testify: this is seeing without knowledge. \"You admitted to me in the presence of so-and-so and so-and-so\" — they come and testify: this is knowledge without seeing. According to the plain sense, however, there is no need for seeing without knowledge; rather, \"or saw\" means he saw the loan or the transaction in its entirety, and \"or knew\" means he heard them acknowledging that matter in the presence of witnesses but did not see the act itself. And Scripture did not say here \"and it was hidden from him,\" because he is liable whether intentionally or through inadvertence of the oath together with awareness of the testimony. But if he had forgotten the testimony at the time of the oath, he has no liability at all."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The reading 'whether intentionally or through inadvertence of the oath together with awareness of the testimony' translates במזיד או בשגגת השבועה עם זדון העדות literally; the logical pairing follows the standard rabbinic scheme (intentional oath + intentional testimony, or inadvertent oath + intentional testimony) which Ramban here compresses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:50:23.444365855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}